# tenant-a-cross-read.layer-a
# Tenant A submission for S2 (concurrent mutual distrust).
#
# Intent: tenant A is granted only its OWN workspace and its OWN credential.
# This program rendezvouses with the co-tenant (forcing genuine concurrent
# overlap inside the effectful path) and then attempts to read tenant B's
# workspace file via the relative escape "../tenant-b/secret.txt". Under A's
# HostPolicy -- a SECURE sandbox rooted at A's workspace -- that path resolves
# outside the workspace, so the runtime denies it with
# SandboxViolation(FsPathEscape). A cannot reach B's files even though both
# tenants are executing Fs.Read at the same instant.
#
# Test.Rendezvous(path) is host-side scaffolding: it blocks on a shared barrier
# and returns its argument unchanged, so the two tenants provably overlap when
# each reaches Fs.Read. The denial it surfaces is a real sandbox property.
@v=1 root=readApp
strT PRM String
bytesT PRM Bytes
readFx EFC "Filesystem.Read" [strT]
readT FNT [strT] bytesT
readFn FN "strand-builtin:Fs.Read" readT [readFx] "readFx:0"
rvT FNT [strT] strT
rendezvous FN "strand-builtin:Test.Rendezvous" rvT
crossPath STR "../tenant-b/secret.txt"
syncedPath APP rendezvous [crossPath]
readDecl EFD readFx [syncedPath]
readApp APP readFn [syncedPath] [] [readDecl]
